From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Benjamin Gregoire <Benjamin.Gregoire@inria.fr>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 18:55:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] armv8a: lower conditional expressions to CSINC, CSINV, CSNEG,
 CSET and CSETM

A word conditional expression whose operands are two registers is lowered
to CSEL. When the second operand is a register incremented by one
(b + 1 or 1 + b), complemented (!b) or negated (-b), and the first one a
register, it is lowered to CSINC, CSINV or CSNEG. When the first operand
is the transformed one, the operands are exchanged and the condition is
negated; assembly generation turns the negation into the inverse
condition code.

The constant selections c ? 1 : 0 and c ? -1 : 0 are lowered to CSET and
CSETM, and c ? 0 : 1 and c ? 0 : -1 to the same instructions under the
negated condition. Constants are recognized at the width of the
expression, both as word conditional expressions and in the form
(ws)(c ? n0 : n1) the front-end gives to an integer conditional
expression at a word type.

(cherry picked from commit fa899395c2daf7e79bbe60aef36e4d8e0dface69)
